{
	"_comment": "Simply Swords (optional: skipped unless it's installed). Its 15 weapon types, made at iron and diamond (its crafting-table recipes; netherite needs the smithing table, not yet). Two-handed: Better Combat's two-handed types. Uniques and runic weapons are loot only; they count as diamond weapons (unique_tier) unless an entry says otherwise. 'ability': when it right-clicks the weapon in a fight (hands/UniqueAbility): when 'crowd' (count enemies within range), 'target' (what it fights is min to max blocks off, in sight), 'hurt' (health at or below that fraction), 'fight' (target within max); 'hold' = ticks held for a charged ability. No ability on purpose: the thrown ones (Frostfall, Livyatan, Wickpiercer, Wraithfang: they return to the thrower, and the thrower would be the Drifter's stand-in player), the dashes, blinks and rides (Storm's Edge, Whisperwind, Stars Edge, Thunderbrand, Dreadwhisper, Shadowsting, Soulstealer, Soulstalker, Gloampiercer: they would move the stand-in, not the Drifter), the ones that spend charges built up while held (Dreadtide, Bloodwake, Ionbound Stormscale, Molten Edge), Soulpyre (it reshapes the ground) and The Devourer (a parry). Those it swings as plain weapons; their on-hit effects still work.",
